2026-07-15 14:22:15,942 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: Based on our company's capabilities and context, we can propose an AI-powered intelligent assistance tool that leverages retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) to support hospital staff in their daily activities. Our approach will utilize a combination of natural language processing (NLP) and machine learning algorithms to provide explainable recommendations and suggestions.

We will employ our core RAG capabilities, including hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, multi-document synthesis, structured extraction, template-guided drafting, applicable rules recall, action and verification suggestions, and dossier-context continuity. These capabilities will enable the tool to retrieve relevant information from the hospital's internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulations, and provide staff with accurate and up-to-date information.

To support drafting of medical and administrative documents, we can utilize our template-guided drafting capability, which allows for the generation of structured documents such as discharge summaries, medical correspondence, and administrative documents. Our tool will also provide suggestions for next steps based on the dossier context and applicable rules, ensuring that staff can efficiently handle dossiers and maintain continuity of care.

In terms of explainability, our solution will provide source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval trace, and every interaction will be logged for a posteriori audit, ensuring transparency and trust in the decision-making process. Our approach is consistent with HAS guidance, which emphasizes human oversight and validation of AI-generated recommendations.

Our innovation strategy will involve an iterative approach, starting with corpus selection and curation with the client's experts, followed by retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and evaluation loop. We will measure answer quality using a labelled evaluation set built with the client, focusing on groundedness, relevance, and factual support.

We can propose either our sovereign European open-weight model or top-tier proprietary models via API, depending on the client's requirements and constraints. Our sovereign model offers strong grounding behavior, explainability, and sovereignty, while our proprietary models provide higher performance on complex drafting and reasoning tasks.

Overall, our proposed solution will deliver an intelligent assistance tool that supports hospital staff in their daily activities, provides explainable recommendations and suggestions, and maintains continuity of care between professionals and services. Our approach is grounded in our company's capabilities and context, ensuring a robust and effective solution that meets the client's requirements and constraints.
