Our solution, Atelier, is designed as an intelligent assistance tool that supports hospital staff in their daily activities. It provides retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities, leveraging natural language processing (NLP) and machine learning algorithms to offer explainable recommendations and suggestions. The tool assists with information retrieval from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulations, drafting of medical and administrative documents, and handling dossiers. It also facilitates continuity of care between professionals, shifts, and services.

To ensure strict compliance with GDPR, we implement measures such as encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, pseudonymisation, and data minimisation techniques to protect sensitive data. Our key management system is based on EU-based infrastructure, and we have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed to oversee data protection activities. We also maintain audit logs of access and system outputs.

Our hosting partner, OuraneCloud, holds the HDS certification, ensuring that health data is hosted exclusively within the European Union and in compliance with French regulations. We do not transfer data outside the EU, adhering to the client's requirement for data sovereignty. The infrastructure hosting our solution meets the requirements for SecNumCloud qualification and HDS certification.

The proposed architecture involves deploying Atelier on the Sovereign HDS tier of OuraneCloud, which meets all requirements related to hosting, performance, integration, and interoperability standards, while ensuring data sovereignty and compliance with regulatory constraints. This setup allows for horizontal scaling to ensure high throughput and maintain the required availability and response times.

Our solution provides response times below 2 seconds for common queries, with a median latency of 1.3 seconds and p95 query time below 2 seconds. The availability target is 99.9%, ensuring continuity of care. We also support health interoperability standards such as HL7/FHIR, INS, and the national framework (Ségur du numérique en santé, Mon espace santé/DMP).

To address environmental concerns, we leverage our existing capabilities as a CSR & Sustainability officer at Faber IA. Our solution is deployed on green hosting infrastructure, with a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2 and heat reuse. We implement digital sobriety practices, including model right-sizing, caching, and batching, to minimize energy consumption and optimize resource utilization.

Our budget proposal is within the client's estimated global budget of €900,000 over five years. We aim to maintain a target gross margin between 25% and 35%, with standard daily rates ranging from €700 to €1,300 per day, excluding VAT. Our financial role works closely with the architect to keep the proposed configuration within the authority's budget envelope while preserving an acceptable margin.

In conclusion, Faber IA's proposal addresses all requirements and constraints outlined in the call for tenders. Our solution, Atelier, provides an intelligent assistance tool that supports hospital staff in their daily activities, ensures strict compliance with GDPR, and meets technical, regulatory, and environmental requirements. We are confident that our team has the necessary expertise and capacity to deliver this project within the proposed timeline and budget.
